(begin-tx "DPB-05 - GS-05: the defpact door with the virtual-gas switch OFF")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [DPB-05 · 01 · flip the switch the defpact used to ignore] ---")
;;<<DPB-05>> GS-05, WHICH THE LEDGER ITSELF RECORDED AS UNTESTABLE AND THEN LEFT UNTESTED.
;;
;;All seven `UDC_ConstructOutputCumulator` calls in 20_MTX-SWP.pact passed a HARDCODED `false` as
;;the `trigger` argument. `trigger` is the virtual-gas-zero switch -- UDC_MakeModularCumulator
;;returns {"ignis": 0.0} when it is true -- and every other cumulator in the codebase passes
;;(ref-IGNIS::URC_IsVirtualGasZero). GS-05 replaced all seven.
;;
;;GS-05's own entry says why nothing caught it: "Invisible to the suite because the toggle is ON in
;;every fixture, so the hardcoded `false` and the real reader return the same value in every test
;;that has ever run." That was true, and it stayed true after the fix -- the repair was shipped with
;;the same blind spot that hid the defect. A CONSTANT THAT HAPPENS TO EQUAL THE EXPRESSION IT
;;REPLACED IS ONLY DETECTABLE BY A TEST THAT VARIES THE EXPRESSION.
;;
;;So this block varies it. With IGNIS collection switched OFF, every door to the operation must go
;;free -- and the defpact door is the one that used to keep charging.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-A:module{TalosStageOne_AdminV2} TS01-A)
        (ref-TS01-CP:module{TalosStageOne_ClientPactsV4} TS01-CP)
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-IGNIS:module{IgnisCollectorV2} IGNIS)
        (patron:string KST.ANHD)
        (pool:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
        (amounts:[decimal] [10.0 10.0 10.0])
    )
    ;;native=false selects the VIRTUAL (IGNIS) collection switch; toggle=false turns it off.
    (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_IgnisToggle false false)
    (let
        (
            ;;the ASYMMETRY TAX, read from the same CLAD reader DPB-01 uses.
            (tax:decimal
                (at "total-ignis-tax-needed"
                    (SWPLC.URCi_AddStandardLiquidityClad patron pool amounts
                        (U|CT.UR_STOA-PID|Price))))
            (quoted:decimal
                (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis"
                    (INFO-ONE.INFO_SWP|AddStandardLiquidity patron patron pool amounts
                        (U|CT.UR_STOA-PID|Price)))))
            (b0:decimal (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false))
        )
        (map print
            [
                ;;the switch really moved -- URC_IsVirtualGasZero is (not UR_VirtualToggle)
                (expect "<<DPB-05>> IGNIS collection is OFF, so URC_IsVirtualGasZero is now true"
                    true (ref-IGNIS::URC_IsVirtualGasZero))
                ;;THE OWNER'S FIRST RULE, UNDER THE SWITCH. This is what the `trigger` field
                ;;actually governs: UDC_MakeModularCumulator reports {"ignis": 0.0} when it is true,
                ;;so the PREVIEW reads zero. The EXEC is zero for a different reason -- C_Collect
                ;;gates on UR_VirtualToggle itself. A hardcoded `false` therefore makes the preview
                ;;quote a cost the chain will not charge.
                (expect "<<DPB-05>> with collection off the PREVIEW also quotes zero, matching the charge"
                    0.0 quoted)
            ])
        (ref-TS01-CP::SWP|C_AddStandardLiquidity patron patron pool amounts)
        (continue-pact 1)
        (continue-pact 2)
        (let
            (
                (total:decimal (- b0 (ref-DALOS::UR_TF_AccountSupply patron false)))
            )
            ;;restore BEFORE asserting, so a failure here cannot leave the switch off for any
            ;;later file that shares this state.
            (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_IgnisToggle false true)
            (map print
                [
                    (format "<<DPB-05>> switch OFF: quoted={} charged={} tax={}" [quoted total tax])
                    ;;THE GS-05 ASSERTION. With the pre-fix hardcoded `false` this is DPB-01's
                    ;;1318.83, not 0.0 -- the single-tx doors would have gone free while this one
                    ;;kept charging full price, which is RT-A-001's shape triggered by an admin
                    ;;action instead of a client choice.
                    ;;THE GS-05 ASSERTION. The GAS goes to zero; the TAX does not, and should not.
                    ;;The first draft asserted total == 0.0 and measured 200.0 -- which is the tax
                    ;;exactly. Reading the code rather than filing a defect: the tax is
                    ;;`TFT::C_Transfer ignis-id account vst-sc ... ` (20_MTX-SWP.pact:935) -- a real
                    ;;transfer of the IGNIS FUNGIBLE to the VST contract, not a gas collection. The
                    ;;virtual-gas switch zeroes GAS; it does not stop asset transfers that happen to
                    ;;be denominated in the gas token. So the correct claim is that the whole
                    ;;1118.83 gas component disappears and only the tax survives.
                    ;;
                    ;;With the pre-GS-05 hardcoded `false` this reads 1318.83 -- gas AND tax -- while
                    ;;the single-tx doors went free: RT-A-001's shape, triggered by an admin action
                    ;;instead of a client choice.
                    (expect "<<DPB-05>> the DEFPACT door's GAS goes to zero; only the asymmetry tax survives"
                        tax total)
                    ;;non-vacuity: a tax of 0 would satisfy the line above against a charge of 0 and
                    ;;prove nothing about the gas component.
                    (expect "<<DPB-05>> ...and that tax is a real, non-zero transfer, so the equality bites"
                        true (> tax 0.0))
                    ;;non-vacuity: the same door, same pool, same amounts, charges 1318.83 with the
                    ;;switch ON -- that is DPB-01 at the top of this file. Asserting the switch came
                    ;;back keeps that claim honest for anything that runs after this.
                    (expect "<<DPB-05>> ...and the switch is back ON, so billing is live again"
                        false (ref-IGNIS::URC_IsVirtualGasZero))
                ])
        )
    )
    ""
)
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(commit-tx)
